import AxQM.Concrete.DeutschReachableUnitary
import AxQM.Postulates.API.QuditGate

/-!
# The reachable `G`-circuit matrices are operators of a register `Evolution` submonoid
(N&C Exercise 4.44, Deutsch-gate universality — the matrix→`Evolution` operator identification)

The matrix development of Exercise 4.44 realises the universality of the Deutsch gate
`G = C²(iR_x(πα))` (with ancillas held `|1⟩`) at the level of raw matrices: the reachable
full-register circuits `deutschAncillaReachableCircuits fullEnc dataEnc e α` — finite products of
ancilla-`|1⟩`-preserving matrices, each a topological limit of `G`-placements on register wires —
compress to a set of data-register actions dense in `U(2ⁿ)` up to a global phase
(`Concrete.exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschDataReachableCircuits`). To lift that density to the
physical gate `deutschGate α` (an `Evolution`), the abstract matrix submonoid must
first be exhibited as the operators of a submonoid of closed-system `Evolution`s of `qudit D`.

This file does exactly that, one operator at a time — the Deutsch-gate counterpart of the
four-gate bridge `exists_reachableCircuitEvolution_op_eq`
(`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReachableCircuit.lean`).

## What is formalised

* `deutschReachableEvolutions fullEnc dataEnc e α` — the **register-level reachable `G`-circuit
  submonoid**: the submonoid of `Evolution (qudit D)` generated by the `quditGate` promotions of
  the reachable ancilla-preserving gates `deutschAncillaReachableGates fullEnc dataEnc e α` (each
  unitary by `Concrete.deutschAncillaReachableGates_subset_unitaryGroup`). Its members are exactly
  the `Evolution`s whose operators are reachable circuit matrices — the register-gate counterpart
  of the matrix submonoid `Concrete.deutschAncillaReachableCircuits`.
* `quditGate_mem_deutschReachableEvolutions` — each generator: `quditGate hN` for a reachable gate
  `N ∈ deutschAncillaReachableGates` is a member. Via the arbitrary-wire naming
  (`quditGate_mcCtrlSingleQubit_distinct_eq_conj_congr_tmul_ccontrolledUnitary`) the
  exact base placements among these generators are the physical Deutsch gate `deutschGate α`
  transported/conjugated onto register wires.
* `exists_deutschReachableEvolution_op_eq` — **the matrix→submonoid bridge (operator form)**: every
  matrix `N ∈ Concrete.deutschAncillaReachableCircuits fullEnc dataEnc e α` is the operator of some
  member `E` of `deutschReachableEvolutions fullEnc dataEnc e α`:

    `E.op = Matrix.toEuclideanCLM N`.

  Proved by `Submonoid.closure_induction` over `deutschAncillaReachableGates`. On a generator `N`,
  its unitarity witness (`Concrete.deutschAncillaReachableGates_subset_unitaryGroup`) makes
  `quditGate hN` a member, with operator `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM N` (`quditGate_op`). The unit is
  `1`; products are carried by the multiplicativity of both `Evolution.op` (`Evolution.comp_op`) and
  `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM` (`map_mul`).

This is the register-side identification used by the density transport of
`AxQM/Postulates/API/DeutschUniversality.lean`: the matrix density statement
`exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschDataReachableCircuits`,
transported through the continuous `⋆`-algebra isomorphism `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM` and the
coordinate-subspace compression, lands in the closure of the operator image of
`deutschReachableEvolutions`, giving the universality of `deutschGate α` with ancillas.
-/

open Matrix

namespace AxQM

noncomputable section

open AxQM.Concrete

/-- **The register-level reachable `G`-circuit submonoid.** The submonoid of `Evolution (qudit D)`
generated by the `quditGate` promotions of the reachable ancilla-preserving gates
`deutschAncillaReachableGates fullEnc dataEnc e α` (each unitary by
`Concrete.deutschAncillaReachableGates_subset_unitaryGroup`, so a `quditGate` exists). Its members
are exactly the `Evolution`s whose operators are reachable circuit matrices
(`exists_deutschReachableEvolution_op_eq`) — the register-gate counterpart of the abstract matrix
submonoid `Concrete.deutschAncillaReachableCircuits fullEnc dataEnc e α`. -/
noncomputable def deutschReachableEvolutions {M m n D d : ℕ} (fullEnc : (Fin M → Fin 2) ≃ Fin D)
    (dataEnc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d) (e : Fin M ≃ Fin m ⊕ Fin n) (α : ℝ) :
    Submonoid (Evolution (qudit D)) :=
  Submonoid.closure
    {E | ∃ (N : Matrix (Fin D) (Fin D) ℂ) (hN : N ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup (Fin D) ℂ),
      N ∈ deutschAncillaReachableGates fullEnc dataEnc e α ∧ E = quditGate hN}

/-- **The `quditGate` of a reachable gate is a generator of the submonoid.** For a reachable
ancilla-preserving gate `N ∈ deutschAncillaReachableGates fullEnc dataEnc e α` (unitary by
`Concrete.deutschAncillaReachableGates_subset_unitaryGroup`), the promotion `quditGate hN` is a
member of `deutschReachableEvolutions fullEnc dataEnc e α`. The exact base placements among these
gates are, by
`quditGate_mcCtrlSingleQubit_distinct_eq_conj_congr_tmul_ccontrolledUnitary`, the physical Deutsch
gate `deutschGate α` conjugated onto register wires. -/
theorem quditGate_mem_deutschReachableEvolutions {M m n D d : ℕ} (fullEnc : (Fin M → Fin 2) ≃ Fin D)
    (dataEnc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d) (e : Fin M ≃ Fin m ⊕ Fin n) (α : ℝ)
    {N : Matrix (Fin D) (Fin D) ℂ}
    (hN : N ∈ deutschAncillaReachableGates fullEnc dataEnc e α) :
    quditGate (deutschAncillaReachableGates_subset_unitaryGroup fullEnc dataEnc e α hN)
      ∈ deutschReachableEvolutions fullEnc dataEnc e α :=
  Submonoid.subset_closure
    ⟨N, deutschAncillaReachableGates_subset_unitaryGroup fullEnc dataEnc e α hN, hN, rfl⟩

/-- **The reachable `G`-circuit matrices are operators of the register circuit submonoid.** Every
matrix `N ∈ Concrete.deutschAncillaReachableCircuits fullEnc dataEnc e α` is the operator of some
member `E` of the register submonoid `deutschReachableEvolutions fullEnc dataEnc e α`:

  `E.op = Matrix.toEuclideanCLM N`.

Proved by `Submonoid.closure_induction` over `deutschAncillaReachableGates`. On a generator `N`, the
unitarity witness (`Concrete.deutschAncillaReachableGates_subset_unitaryGroup`) makes `quditGate hN`
a member with operator `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM N` (`quditGate_op`); the unit maps to `1`
(`Evolution.id_op`, `map_one`); products are carried by the multiplicativity of both `Evolution.op`
(`Evolution.comp_op`) and `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM` (`map_mul`). The Deutsch-gate counterpart of
`exists_reachableCircuitEvolution_op_eq`. -/
theorem exists_deutschReachableEvolution_op_eq {M m n D d : ℕ} {fullEnc : (Fin M → Fin 2) ≃ Fin D}
    {dataEnc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d} {e : Fin M ≃ Fin m ⊕ Fin n} {α : ℝ}
    {N : Matrix (Fin D) (Fin D) ℂ}
    (hN : N ∈ deutschAncillaReachableCircuits fullEnc dataEnc e α) :
    ∃ E ∈ deutschReachableEvolutions fullEnc dataEnc e α,
      E.op = Matrix.toEuclideanCLM (𝕜 := ℂ) (n := Fin D) N := by
  induction hN using Submonoid.closure_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    have hxu := deutschAncillaReachableGates_subset_unitaryGroup fullEnc dataEnc e α hx
    exact ⟨quditGate hxu, quditGate_mem_deutschReachableEvolutions fullEnc dataEnc e α hx,
      quditGate_op hxu⟩
  | one =>
    refine ⟨1, one_mem _, ?_⟩
    rw [Evolution.one_def, Evolution.id_op]
    exact (map_one Matrix.toEuclideanCLM).symm
  | mul x y _ _ ihx ihy =>
    obtain ⟨Ex, hEx, hExop⟩ := ihx
    obtain ⟨Ey, hEy, hEyop⟩ := ihy
    refine ⟨Ex * Ey, mul_mem hEx hEy, ?_⟩
    rw [Evolution.mul_def, Evolution.comp_op, hExop, hEyop]
    exact (map_mul Matrix.toEuclideanCLM x y).symm

end

end AxQM
